  "reference_protocol": "Each complete SQL statement goes to both public file modes and the pinned SQLite shell. Compare output, return code, normalized diagnostic and persisted catalog/rowids/rows/integrity. Source omitted versus explicit targets remain actual parsed information, never inferred from an expected result.",
  "implementation": "RowPreparation now carries an explicit physical target compiler as well as its typed row callback. InsertTargets retains the source implicit-width property through VALUES, SELECT, private materialization, streaming registers and UPSERT. Shared input checks run before expression evaluation and distinguish omitted lists from explicit lists. Ordinary SELECT input mismatches use SQLite explicit-list wording. A shared function registry fallback operates on the prepared scalar tree after the existing resolver; internal affinity annotations remain structurally transparent, original DISTINCT spelling is kept, and ignored ORDER syntax is prepared away as before.",
  "proof_scope": "The default ordinary-target compiler has a registered identity contract; the internal affinity annotation has a registered function-lookup component contract. The new runtime unit group checks source AST provenance, exact mismatch diagnostics and binding/width order. Earlier raw Core command/row proof domains are retained. No general equivalence theorem for all INSERT preparation priorities is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh-seed survey share named families and one generator. Their 16 failures are not a global compatibility percentage.",
